filter.description:
Optional filter expressed as a JSON string following the Notion filter format (https://developers.notion.com/reference/filter-data-source-entries). Each filter targets one property by name and applies a type-specific condition. Common patterns:
- Status: {"property":"Status","status":{"equals":"In progress"}}
- Checkbox: {"property":"Done","checkbox":{"equals":true}}
- Text contains: {"property":"Name","rich_text":{"contains":"keyword"}}
- Date after: {"property":"Due","date":{"after":"2024-01-01"}}
- Compound (AND): {"and":[{...},{...}]}
- Compound (OR): {"or":[{...},{...}]}
Always call getDataSource first to discover the available property names and their types before constructing a filter. Omit to return all rows up to pageSize.

